<title>FRANCE: New York main origin for Paris air imports in H1,.</title>
<headline>New York main origin for Paris air imports in H1,.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, said New York was the top airport origin for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports in January-June 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten orignating airport gateways for the Paris airports, in tonnes, with percentage changes from H1 '96 were:</p>
<p>	Origin    Jan-June '97  Pct Change</p>
<p>  1.  New York	18,002   down  12.4</p>
<p>  2.  Chicago	 14,045   down   2.5</p>
<p>  3.  Tokyo	   10,843   up    44.4</p>
<p>  4.  Hong Kong	9,663   up    14.6</p>
<p>  5.  Montreal	 7,555   down   4.4</p>
<p>  6.  Los Angeles    7,265   down  15.9</p>
<p>  7.  Bangkok	  6,737   up    33.6</p>
<p>  8.  Singapore	4,524   up    89.8</p>
<p>  9.  Miami	    3,484   down   6.5</p>
<p> 10.  Buenos Aires   3,337   up     1.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
